<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>NAWI Test Report Generator</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>

<body>
    <nav class="navbar">
        <a href="/" class="navbar-brand">
            <img src="/images/logo.jpg" alt="Bytebrigade Logo">
            Bytebrigade
        </a>
        <div class="navbar-links">
            <a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Home</a>
            <a href="/new-test"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> New Test</a>
            <a href="/dashboard"><i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i> Dashboard</a>
        </div>
    </nav>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="hero">
            <img src="/images/hero.jpg" alt="Analytical Balance in Laboratory">
            <h1>NAWI Test Report Generator</h1>
            <p>A comprehensive testing suite for Non-Automatic Weighing Instruments in compliance with OIML standards.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
            <a href="/new-test"><button class="btn"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Start New Test</button></a>
            <a href="/dashboard"><button class="btn btn-secondary"><i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i> View
                    Dashboard</button></a>
        </div>

        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="icon-wrapper"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale"></i></div>
                <h4>Weighing Performance</h4>
                <p>Automatically calculates Maximum Permissible Error (MPE) thresholds based on the instrument's
                    accuracy class, capacity, and verification scale interval (e).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="icon-wrapper"><i class="fas fa-sync-alt"></i></div>
                <h4>Repeatability</h4>
                <p>Ensures that the instrument provides consistent results when the same load is applied under identical
                    environmental conditions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="info-card">
                <div class="icon-wrapper"><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i></div>
                <h4>Eccentricity</h4>
                <p>Verifies the accuracy of the instrument when a load is placed in different positions (center,
                    front-left, back-right, etc.) on the load receptor.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>

</html>